  "summary": "Proposed a 12-round hard cap with cycle-based early termination (evaluate every 3-4 rounds) as the best balance of convergence opportunity and cost control. Suggested replacing subjective 'should we continue?' verdicts with two binary questions — 'are new points emerging?' and 'are positions converging?' — which map to four clear states (progress, healthy debate, consensus, stall) and are harder for an LLM to game with optimism bias. Recommended a structural 'novelty ratio' safeguard that triggers stall detection when fewer than ~20% of points are new for two consecutive evaluation checkpoints, providing a mechanical backstop independent of LLM judgment."
